{
  "_comment": [
    "Viam 103 bimanual QC cell. Two ur5e arms inspect a 60 mm carton: arm-a picks it off",
    "the infeed belt and presents five faces to inspect-cam, hands it to arm-b, and arm-b",
    "places it in the good or bad tray.",
    "",
    "Geometry is the isaac-arcade layout scaled by 0.62, the scale probes/scale_study.py",
    "found: every station stays inside the ur5e's 0.85 m reach with ~10% margin, and both",
    "trays stay OUTSIDE it from arm-a, which is what makes the handoff mandatory rather",
    "than merely intended. Rescaling this cell without re-running that sweep will quietly",
    "break one of those two constraints - the viable window is only 0.58-0.62 wide.",
    "",
    "Each arm's isaac 'position' and its viam 'frame.translation' describe the same point",
    "in two units (m and mm). They MUST agree: the motion service plans against the frame",
    "system, so a disagreement plans collision-free paths through a world that is not the",
    "one being simulated. tests/test_qc_cell_config.py asserts it.",
    "",
    "Belt and tray solids are provisional - sized by eye, not yet re-derived from the",
    "scaled layout."
  ],
